%% Hit-test candidate resolution sequence
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber

  actor Caller as Pointer hit-test caller
  participant Surface as CanvasSurface
  participant Interaction as InteractionEngine
  participant ReadPort as InteractionReadPort
  participant Spatial as SpatialKernel
  participant Store as DocumentStoreKernel
  participant Geometry as GeometryPolicy
  participant Hit as HitTestPolicy
  participant Diagnostics as DiagnosticsHub planned routes

  Caller->>Surface: hit-test request(point hit)
  Surface->>Interaction: normalized finite CanvasPointerSample or finite query envelope
  Interaction->>Spatial: queryHitCandidates(content hit scope, finite envelope, captured structuralRevision)
  Spatial->>Spatial: revision/generation gate

  alt spatial query budget exceeded
    Spatial-->>Interaction: typed budget-exceeded result with no partial candidates
    Interaction->>Diagnostics: planned P10 interaction reliability diagnostic for user-facing budget event
    Interaction-->>Surface: no hit result, no partial candidates consumed
  else bounded candidate handles returned
    Spatial-->>Interaction: candidate handles(id, generation, orderToken, structuralRevision)
    loop handles in reverse layer order and reverse element order
      Note over Interaction: orderToken is the committed ordering fact used to preserve hit priority.
      Interaction->>ReadPort: resolve hit candidate handle
      ReadPort->>Store: resolve handle by id, generation, orderToken, structuralRevision
      alt candidate is stale
        Store-->>ReadPort: stale candidate rejected
        ReadPort-->>Interaction: stale candidate rejected
        Interaction->>Diagnostics: planned P10 interaction reliability diagnostic for stale candidate rejection
      else candidate is current
        Store-->>ReadPort: immutable hit row and common flags
        ReadPort-->>Interaction: immutable hit row and common flags
        Interaction->>Hit: check hit eligibility(point finite, visible, selectable, transform finite)
        Hit->>Geometry: exact family hit with transform, local bounds, hit padding, and slop
        alt committed row has non-invertible transform
          Geometry->>Diagnostics: planned P8 spatial corrupted-row diagnostic
          Geometry-->>Hit: miss
          Hit-->>Interaction: continue candidate scan
        else transform invertible
        alt exact hit accepts visible selectable content element
          Geometry-->>Hit: exact hit accepted
          Hit-->>Interaction: first exact hit wins
          Interaction-->>Surface: hit result for resolved element id
        else not eligible or exact miss
          Geometry-->>Hit: miss
          Hit-->>Interaction: continue candidate scan
        end
        end
      end
    end
  end

  Note over Interaction,ReadPort: Hit-test resolves committed rows through read-only candidate handles only.
  Note over Hit,Geometry: Background elements are not pointer-selectable in v1.
  Note over Caller,Hit: Marquee selection uses the same bounded spatial candidate rules, but selection accumulation is covered by seq_marquee_select.
  Note over Spatial,Hit: Legacy SceneNode traversal and legacy scene order logic are not normative input.
